== REQ-S07-007 USER DG4 | Compute RAG from the approved expected trajectory with configurable thresholds and never from project task completion
  proc: RAG = evaluation of actual versus expected-to-date by polarity using configured thresholds; task completion is not an input
  acc: A04;A05: with all tasks complete and actual below the red threshold the KPI is Red; changing the threshold version recomputes RAG
== REQ-PB-063 SOURCE DG4 | Apply the area-specific T10 RAG logic
  proc: Each area computes status by its own rule; outcome RAG never uses task completion; missing data shows Unknown/Stale
  acc: A04;A05: an outcome whose tasks are 100% complete but KPI is below trajectory is Red/Amber, not Green; a KPI with no actual shows Unknown
== REQ-S03-003 USER DG4 | Keep initiative delivery, business adoption, validated value and transformation closure as separate statuses
  proc: Each status has its own state machine and owner; none is derived from another; views show all four side by side
  acc: A11: setting delivery to Complete leaves adoption, validated value and closure unchanged; the API rejects a closure request while validated value is pending unless a transition decision exists
== REQ-S08-001 USER DG4 | Track planned, forecast, measured, submitted-for-validation, validated, rejected and sustained benefit values separately
  proc: Each benefit keeps separate value series per state; aggregations never combine states
  acc: A10: a forecast amount never appears in the validated total; a rejected measurement is retained and shown as rejected
== REQ-S20-010 ENGINEERING DG4 | Deliver and pass the executable acceptance test A10 Benefit integrity
  proc: qa-verifier derives an executable test (unit;integration) from the scenario and runs it against the gate candidate, recording the command, environment and actual result in test-evidence
  acc: A10: A shared benefit rolls up once; 110% allocation is rejected; unvalidated or forecast value cannot appear as validated actual
== REQ-PB-013 SOURCE DG4 | Restrict Finance / Value Office validation of baseline, benefit logic and value realization to the Finance role
  proc: Only users holding FIN on the transformation can mark a baseline, benefit formula or realized value as validated; others can submit for validation
  acc: A10;A12: a Business Owner calling the validate endpoint receives 403; a Finance user succeeds and the audit event records validator identity
== REQ-S08-003 USER DG4 | Record for each benefit a unique ID, type, accountable business owner, Finance validator where applicable, baseline/counterfactual, formula, driver units, target, timing, one-off/recurring classification, currency, measurement source, evidence, confidence, assumptions, contribution links and financial-statement mapping or agreed non-financial KPI
  proc: Benefit profile form with server-side validation of required fields
  acc: A10: a financial benefit without a financial-statement mapping, or a non-financial one without an agreed KPI, is rejected
== REQ-PB-058 SOURCE DG4 | Prevent double counting: each benefit has a unique owner, baseline, formula and financial-statement or non-financial KPI link
  proc: System rejects a benefit without a single owner, baseline, formula and a financial statement line or agreed non-financial KPI; initiatives link to canonical benefits via allocations, parent/child relationships and shared-benefit groups; portfolio totals sum canonical benefits, not links, so a shared benefit rolls up once
  acc: A10: a benefit with two owners is rejected; a 10 million SAR benefit shared by two initiatives appears once (10 million SAR) in the portfolio total
== REQ-S08-013 USER DG4 | Reject allocations over 100% and show any share below 100% as unallocated
  proc: The server sums allocations per benefit; above 100% is rejected; below 100% shows the remaining share as unallocated
  acc: A10: allocations 60% + 50% are rejected; 60% + 30% saves and shows 10% unallocated
== REQ-PB-015 SOURCE DG4 | Model the six stage gates G1-G6 as explicit approval records with decision question and evidence required
  proc: Owner assembles evidence, submits the gate; approver records decision against the evidence snapshot; gates are never inferred from task completion
  acc: A08: submission with missing mandatory evidence is rejected; approval by a non-approver returns 403; approval of a stale submission version is rejected
== REQ-S04-002 USER DG4 | Make gates explicit approval records tied to a versioned, immutable evidence snapshot, never inferred from task completion
  proc: Submitting a gate freezes the linked evidence record versions into a snapshot; approvers decide on that snapshot; completing all tasks never changes gate state
  acc: A07;A08: completing every phase task leaves the gate Draft; editing a record after submission does not change the snapshot content shown to approvers
== REQ-PB-021 SOURCE DG4 | G6 Sustain: require benefits evidence, ownership transfer, controls and continuous improvement backlog as gate evidence
  proc: G6 checklist links validated benefit evidence, accepted BAU handover, controls and the CI backlog
  acc: A08;A11: G6 submission without an accepted BAU handover is rejected listing 'Ownership transfer'
== REQ-DLV-002 ENGINEERING DG0 | Keep engineering delivery gates DG0-DG7 separate from product business approvals G1-G6 in records, authority and meaning
  proc: DG records live only under docs/delivery; G1-G6 are product records; project rules and every agent definition state that an engineering agent cannot grant a real business, Finance or IT approval
  acc: A23;A28: gate records validate only with stage_id DG0-DG7; CLAUDE.md and agent-protocol.md state that G6 never implies DG7 and that no agent grants a business, Finance or IT approval
